  "notes": "Plain's public API is GraphQL-only (core-api.uk.plain.com/graphql/v1). Credentials are created self-serve via Settings → Machine Users → API Keys, scoped with fine-grained permissions, no admin/partner approval documented. Product access is a 7-day free trial (no credit card) then paid seats starting at $35/seat/month; API/webhooks/events are listed under 'Extensibility' without an explicit paid-tier gate, but sustained use requires converting to a paid plan after trial. Plain also ships an official, vendor-maintained MCP server (mcp.plain.com) authenticated via the user's own Plain account session rather than API keys, exposing ~30 tools over threads/customers/tenants/help-center/workspace data.",
